    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
    <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <p>&ldquo;11 months&rdquo; is exact. &ldquo;1 year&rdquo; is exact on 15 March and 20 days short on 4 April. Both labels come from the same code, and they look the same.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l" id="same-label">Same label, different meanings</h2>

  <table class="nhsuk-table-responsive" role="table">
    <caption class="nhsuk-table__caption">
      What each label could mean under each rule
      <span class="nhsuk-body-s nhsuk-u-display-block nhsuk-u-margin-top-2 nhsuk-u-font-weight-normal">Truncated: any units that are not shown are dropped. Ages are never rounded. Precision the reader can see: the smallest unit the label proves was counted.</span>
    </caption>
    <thead class="nhsuk-table__head" role="rowgroup">
      <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Displayed</th>
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Could mean (truncated)</th>
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Exact meaning</th>
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Precision the reader can see</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="nhsuk-table__body">
      <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
        <th scope="row" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="rowheader">11 months</th>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Could mean (truncated) </span><span>11 months 0 days up to the day before 12 months (11 months 27 to 30 days, depending on month lengths)</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Exact meaning </span><span>11 months 0 days</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Precision the reader can see </span><span>None. The days might have been dropped, or might have been 0 and left out.</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
        <th scope="row" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="rowheader">3 years 4 months</th>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Could mean (truncated) </span><span>3 years 4 months 0 days up to the day before 3 years 5 months</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Exact meaning </span><span>3 years 4 months 0 days</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Precision the reader can see </span><span>None. The days might have been dropped, or might have been 0 and left out.</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
        <th scope="row" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="rowheader">3 years 4 months 0 days</th>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Could mean (truncated) </span><span>3 years 4 months 0 days only, because days are shown</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Exact meaning </span><span>3 years 4 months 0 days, although which day counts as &ldquo;4 months&rdquo; can still depend on month-end rules</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Precision the reader can see </span><span>Days. The &ldquo;0 days&rdquo; shows days were counted.</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
        <th scope="row" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="rowheader">3 years 0 months 0 days</th>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Could mean (truncated) </span><span>The third birthday only</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Exact meaning </span><span>The third birthday</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Precision the reader can see </span><span>Days. The zeros show months and days were counted.</span></td>
      </tr>
      <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
        <th scope="row" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="rowheader">1 year</th>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Could mean (truncated) </span><span>1 year 0 months 0 days up to the day before 1 year 1 month. If only the largest unit is shown, anything up to the day before the second birthday.</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Exact meaning </span><span>The first birthday</span></td>
        <td class="nhsuk-table__cell" role="cell"><span class="nhsuk-table-responsive__heading" aria-hidden="true">Precision the reader can see </span><span>None. Months and days might have been dropped, or might both have been 0 and left out.</span></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
    <div class="nhsuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <p>Once every unit is shown, zeros included, nothing can have been dropped, so the label is exact and the reader can see that it is. The longer labels remove the ambiguity, at the cost of being longer to read.</p>

      <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l" id="mmr-dose-1">Where it matters: MMR dose 1</h2>

      <p>MMR dose 1 counts as valid only if it is given on or after the first birthday (to confirm against the Green Book).</p>

      <p>All the examples below use a child born on 15 March 2025. Their first birthday is 15 March 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table class="nhsuk-table-responsive" role="table">
    <caption class="nhsuk-table__caption">
      MMR dose 1 for a child born on 15 March 2025
    </caption>
    <thead class="nhsuk-table__head" role="rowgroup">
      <tr class="nhsuk-table__row" role="row">
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Vaccination date</th>
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Exact age</th>
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Shown truncated</th>
        <th scope="col" class="nhsuk-table__header" role="columnheader">Valid dose 1?</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="nhsuk-table__body">
